# Repo-root ignores.
#
# The Unity project is NOT here — it is the "unity/" subfolder, which has
# its own .gitignore. This file guards the repo root instead.
#
# Why it exists: pointing Unity Hub at this folder instead of "unity/"
# does not raise an error. Unity quietly creates a brand new, empty project right
# here — Assets/, Library/, ProjectSettings/ and the rest — and you end up staring
# at an empty editor wondering where the game went. It happened on 2026-09-25.
# Every pattern below is anchored with a leading slash so it applies only to the
# repo root and never to the real project's files.

# A stray Unity project accidentally created at the repo root
/Assets/
/Library/
/Logs/
/Temp/
/Obj/
/Packages/
/ProjectSettings/
/UserSettings/
/MemoryCaptures/
/Recordings/
/Build/
/Builds/

# IDE and solution files generated beside a stray project
/.vsconfig
/.vs/
/*.sln
/*.slnx
/*.csproj
/*.unityproj
/*.user
/*.suo

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
